{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on b174277f: accepted. Assemble privately, then guard once.\n\nThe engine assembles the context and its details from raw objects.\nThe guard wraps the completed public context one time, at the\ncapability invocation. The client replaces its context copy with a\nforwarding facade. Five conditions hold.\n\n1. The private assembly reads no unrepresented value. It copies\n   descriptors and calls no getter. Named case: a capability rule that\n   skips intent runs with zero calls of the lazy intent getter, and\n   its answer equals the runtime's.\n2. No raw reference leaves through the public context. The guard\n   covers intent, fields, from, the view and each nested value, with\n   the descriptor rule of 34fb3c6d. Named case: a walk of the public\n   context by Reflect.ownKeys and descriptor reads finds each\n   unrepresented value unavailable, and each represented descriptor\n   equal to the runtime's.\n3. The facade forwards. It keeps the receiver, the lazy intent, each\n   descriptor kind and attribute, and an absent optional port stays\n   absent for the `in` operator.\n4. The runtime's own judgment builds no guard. The oracle and its\n   4,029 answers stay unchanged.\n5. A guard's target holds no frozen or nonwritable raw value that the\n   trap must then report. The mirror constraints of your report hold.\n\nTwo limits stay, and no source changes for them in E1.\n- hold.ts:329 reads each ref of the export item. It is unavailable\n  when that item holds an unrepresented ref. No shipped application\n  declares hold.\n- A prepared rule hashes its whole input, so a dependent exploration\n  with a pending output in that input is unavailable. Your count: 16\n  Grow forms in the demo, one Lending form and six Counter forms.\n\nI add both limits and this cut to section 5.4 in the amendment after\nE1, and I give the counts to the review after E3. The five cases and\none control of 34fb3c6d stay owed, with the two cases above.","body":{"to":